            <ArticleTitle>Herniation of the left atrial appendage due to partial congenital absence of the left pericardium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Partial congenital absence of the left pericardium is a rare abnormality which may provoke serious complications. We report the case of a young adult, suffering from chest pain due to incarceration of atrial tissue. Based on this case report the clinical, pathophysiological and diagnostic features of this condition are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
